ition/participants/4","/citations/9","document:line:121"],"concerns":["Check that acceptance criteria map to feasible evidence covering release automation and exact-candidate qualification, including malicious inputs, mismatch cases, and lifecycle tests.","Assess whether the alternatives and chosen approach align with the stated scope and stakeholder requirements.","Inspect the generated sequence companion and rendering against its definition and the contract flow; record any rendering verification limit."],"dependsOn":["release-supply","install-lifecycle"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"standalone-scope-and-repository-fit","title":"Standalone scope, context, and repository evidence","selectors":["/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10"],"concerns":["Check the standalone scope and non-goals against captured requirements and the cited repository implementation, including whether existing behavior is accurately characterized.","Assess traceability and repository convention fit for Node/runtime packaging, release operations, and the unchanged IPC and source-install paths.","No upstream HLD or other required references are declared; do not infer missing ancestry."],"dependsOn":["release-supply","install-lifecycle"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"final-consistency","title":"Cross-chunk requirement and contract consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Check complete coverage of the LLD requirements and acceptance claims across all substantive chunks.","Resolve cross-chunk consistency of artifact identity, manifest trust, compatibility, opt-in behavior, error handling, migration, and rollback contracts against the standalone scope and repository evidence.","Check that the sequence artifact, tests, and acceptance mappings support the same end-to-end flow without contradictory assumptions."],"dependsOn":["release-supply","install-lifecycle","verification-and-design-evidence","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Selectors are assigned to substantive chunks by implementation responsibility and evidence type. Shared contract, citation, and sequence-definition units are included in each relevant assessment where they bear on both release production and installation. Every inventory unit is covered by at least one substantive chunk; the final consistency chunk depends on all substantive assessments and does not substitute for them.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"final-consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["release-supply"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["release-supply","install-lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["release-supply","install-lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["release-supply"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["release-supply","verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["release-supply","verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["release-supply","verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["release-supply","verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","verification-and-design-evidence"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["release-supply","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["release-supply","install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["install-lifecycle","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["release-supply","standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["standalone-scope-and-repository-fit"]},{"unitId":"document:line:121","chunkIds":["verification-and-design-evidence"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":4,"retriesUsed":3,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Unit /body/alternativesConsidered lacks matching substantive coverage"},{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Unknown/duplicate selectors in verification"},{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Unit /body/interactionWithShared lacks matching substantive coverage"}],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"release-supply","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"install-lifecycle","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"verification-and-design-evidence","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"standalone-scope-and-repository-fit","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"final-consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"macos-prebuilt-8a036e64","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-8a036e6436ae82ab-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":5,"LOW":1},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"release-supply","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD consistently describes a build → local qualification → protected promotion flow that reuses the exact candidate identity, and its stakeholder citation is reflected in the stated division of work. However, the qualification record and approval handoff lack a defined, verifiable contract, and the diagram’s actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"release-supply-qualification-binding","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md §2.2–2.3, §3.1–3.2","message":"Promotion requires an “approved qualification record” and says it verifies the artifact against that approval, but the LLD specifies neither the record’s schema and trusted storage/transport nor how approval is authenticated and bound to the run ID, artifact ID, and digest. The candidate identity alone does not define evidence that the protected workflow can verify. Consequently, the central local-qualification gate is not implementable or auditable from this contract, despite the manifest’s specified signature binding the manifest to the archive.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.2: qualification returns a generic “release qualification record” and records pass evidence without defining its contract.","LLD.md §2.3: promotion consumes an “approved qualification record” and verifies against it, without specifying approval provenance or qualification-record verification.","LLD.md §3.1–3.2: candidate identity and signed manifest fields are described, but neither defines a qualification evidence or approval binding.","scripts/prepare-source-release.mjs: the existing source-release promotion contract validates concrete evidence files and their hashes against commit/tree; it does not define the new archive candidate qualification record."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","LLD.md §2.1–2.4","LLD.md §3.1–3.2","LLD.md §4–6","LLD.md §9 citations c2, c3, c11","sequence-diagram.html Mermaid source","scripts/prepare-source-release.mjs","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts",".github/workflows/ci.yml"],"limitations":["Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; only its HTML and Mermaid source were inspected."],"advice":["Define the qualification evidence record and approval contract, including trusted provenance, immutable or authenticated transport, and explicit binding to the candidate run ID, artifact ID, and archive digest."]},{"chunkId":"install-lifecycle","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD recognizes the main lifecycle safeguards: opt-in staging, trust and digest checks before extraction, compatibility preflight, retained predecessor pins, and journaled activation with bounded readiness checks. However, the installation contract does not define the concrete prebuilt archive verification and extraction boundary or how its manifest compatibility metadata feeds the existing managed update and recovery contracts. The sequence companion’s rendered visual was not verified.","findings":[{"id":"install-lifecycle-prebuilt-contract","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md §2.4, §3.2, §5, §7","message":"The stage contract promises a signed prebuilt archive will enter the managed lifecycle, but leaves the critical install-side contract underspecified: it does not say which trusted verifier validates the manifest schema, version/sequence floor and compatibility claims, how those claims become the exact predecessor/candidate pair required by managed activation, or what archive entry types and filesystem checks extraction permits. The existing managed update path is built around a qualified checkout and checks exact compatibility pairs and pinned release inventories before cutover; a new archive path needs to specify how it satisfies those same gates. Without that mapping, safe extraction, compatibility admission, and rollback cannot be implemented or audited from this LLD.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.4 only lists broad verification and staging preconditions; it does not define archive format, verifier interface, extraction rules, or metadata-to-compatibility mapping.","LLD.md §3.2 names manifest fields and detached signature but does not define parsing/sequence-floor enforcement or how compatibility metadata becomes a qualified pair.","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts: stageManagedRelease expects a clean checkout, qualified release profiles and exact prior/candidate compatibility, then pins runtime inventory.","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts: recordManagedUpdatePins and stageManagedUpdate durably record release pins and compatibility before changing the predecessor.","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: rollback verifies pinned release inventory and restores selector, service/job, and prior generation through journaled steps.","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts: current bootstrap authenticates source release authorization and persists sequence floors; the LLD does not specify how the new archive verifier integrates with these safeguards."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/citations/0","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-prebuilt-8a036e64.json","LLD.md §2.4, §3.2, §5, §7","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/fresh-managed-activation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts","sequence-diagram.html Mermaid source"],"limitations":["Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; only the HTML companion/source was inspected."],"advice":["Specify the archive format and exact validation/extraction rules, identify the verifier and trust/sequence-floor boundary, map manifest compatibility claims into the existing qualified predecessor/candidate and pin contracts, and state which journaled activation and recovery path handles the staged release."]},{"chunkId":"verification-and-design-evidence","status":"incomplete","summary":"The test strategy and alternatives support the chosen build-once, locally qualified candidate flow, but the security and lifecycle claims are not mapped to sufficiently specific negative tests. The sequence companion source matches the stated flow, but I could not verify its rendered diagram.","findings":[{"id":"verification-negative-case-coverage","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md §5–6, especially the ac3 acceptance mapping","message":"The LLD claims signature, schema, target, sequence, digest, and unsafe-entry checks, but the test plan names only general malicious-manifest, archive-entry, and digest-mismatch fixtures. It does not identify evidence for signature tampering, unsupported targets, sequence rollback/replay, or traversal and link entries. The broad ac3 mapping (“promotion mismatch and rejected archive negative tests”) does not show that these distinct fail-closed conditions are covered, leaving key security acceptance claims without traceable proof.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §5: invalid-manifest error handling claims signature, schema, platform, sequence, and digest checks before extraction.","LLD.md §5 edge cases: archive paths or links leaving staging must be rejected.","LLD.md §6 contract subjects name general malicious-manifest, archive-entry, and digest-mismatch fixtures without enumerating those cases.","LLD.md §6 acceptance mapping for ac3 names only general promotion-mismatch and rejected-archive negative tests."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/companions","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/citations/9","document:line:121","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","LLD.md §5–6","sequence-diagram.html Mermaid source",".github/workflows/ci.yml","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-8a036e6436ae82ab-s1.json"],"limitations":["Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; I inspected its HTML and Mermaid source only."],"advice":["List concrete qualification and rejection cases under the test subjects and map each security and lifecycle claim to its proving test. The alternatives and chosen approach are consistent with the stakeholder constraint to qualify locally and publish the exact candidate."]},{"chunkId":"standalone-scope-and-repository-fit","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD keeps the opt-in prebuilt path distinct from the existing source installer, but its acceptance mapping is not traceable to stated criteria, and its declared bootstrap call site currently handles signed source releases rather than prebuilt archives. The sequence diagram’s rendering could not be verified, so this review is incomplete.","findings":[{"id":"standalone-acceptance-traceability","severity":"MED","location":"LLD §6, Acceptance mapping","message":"The mapping uses ac1–ac3 without defining their acceptance text in the LLD or the captured scope. The cited stakeholder request specifies local qualification and GitHub-based build/sign/publication, but does not define these three criteria. As written, reviewers cannot determine whether each criterion is fully covered by its listed proving tests or whether requirements are omitted.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §6: acceptance mapping lists ac1–ac3 with test names but no criterion text","Canonical artifact body.testStrategy.acceptanceMapping","Canonical artifact citations[10]: stakeholder request states release qualification is local and GitHub Actions handles build, signing, and publication"]},{"id":"bootstrap-callsite-source-prebuilt-mismatch","severity":"MED","location":"LLD §3.2, Signed release manifest v1 — Call sites","message":"The only declared call site, `src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts`, currently authenticates a signed Git source-release tag and authorizes a Git checkout. It does not verify a detached signature over an archive manifest or validate/extract a prebuilt archive. The design should specify how this call site will support the new archive contract, or identify a prebuilt-specific entry point, so the proposed manifest contract does not appear to be implemented by an incompatible existing bootstrap.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §3.2: manifest claims a detached project signature over archive metadata and names `src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts` as its call site","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts:11, 99–151 — source-release verifier, signed Git tag, candidate branch head, and source-release receipt","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts:154–160 — checks out the authorized source release"]},{"id":"standalone-hld-provenance-conflict","severity":"LOW","location":"LLD Summary and §1 HLD context","message":"The document gives an HLD base run and effective hash in its summary, while §1 says this standalone feature has no parent HLD and no shared HLD contracts. Clarify whether those values are workflow provenance or an upstream design reference; the current wording makes the standalone context difficult to trace.","evidenceReferences":["LLD Summary: HLD base run `wf-1794638228206-o4i31o` and effective hash","LLD §1: “Standalone feature — no parent HLD.”","Canonical artifact meta: `standalone: true` with populated `hldBaseRunId` and `hldEffectiveHash`"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","scripts/prepare-source-release.mjs","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/fresh-managed-activation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts",".github/workflows/ci.yml","docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/sequence-diagram.html","README.md","docs/daemon.md","package.json",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-8a036e6436ae82ab-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-prebuilt-8a036e64.json"],"limitations":["The sequence diagram HTML was inspected as source, but the browser access host was unavailable, so its rendered appearance and layout could not be verified."],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"final-consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD and sequence source describe the same broad build → local qualification → protected promotion → opt-in installation flow. The cross-chunk gaps already identified remain material: the qualification approval is not bound by a defined verifiable contract, and the archive verification and compatibility claims are not mapped into the managed lifecycle. I could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered appearance.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-prebuilt-8a036e64.json","LLD.md §2–7","docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/sequence-diagram.html: Mermaid sequence source","src/bin/insrc-release-bootstrap.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts"],"limitations":["The sequence diagram’s rendered appearance and layout could not be verified; only its HTML and Mermaid source were inspected."],"advice":["See the existing findings `release-supply-qualification-binding`, `install-lifecycle-prebuilt-contract`, `verification-negative-case-coverage`, `standalone-acceptance-traceability`, and `bootstrap-callsite-source-prebuilt-mismatch`; this consistency pass found no separate issue to add."]}],"limitations":["Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; only its HTML and Mermaid source were inspected.","Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; only the HTML companion/source was inspected.","Could not verify the sequence diagram’s rendered visual; I inspected its HTML and Mermaid source only.","The sequence diagram HTML was inspected as source, but the browser access host was unavailable, so its rendered appearance and layout could not be verified.","The sequence diagram’s rendered appearance and layout could not be verified; only its HTML and Mermaid source were inspected."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"50227a472660f3c2ab3ee9deb4372b0e4eb8dd0a415d8d7f28b4ee976a140252"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-14T06:45:51.873Z","publication":{"reviewId":"macos-prebuilt-8a036e64","attempt":1,"state":"pending"},"submitted":{"artifactPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/pilot-prebuilt-macos-daemon-releases-E202611148a036e64/S001/LLD.md","attempt":1},"actionId":"start-1","operation":"start","acceptedAt":"2026-11-14T06:39:02.843Z","resourceGuard":{"daemonInstance":"997f2bb6-492d-401b-a8ae-727ecaa191c1","openLeases":[]}}],"admissionFailures":[]}}}}
